# Argosy Tides - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
Maritime trading simulation game | Unreal Engine 5.4+ | C++20, Blueprint, Rust, Python

## Current State
**Phase 0:** ✅ Foundation Complete  
**Next:** Phase 1 (MVP) - One port, one ship, one commodity loop

## Tech Stack
- **C++20** - Core game systems (Unreal Engine native)
- **Blueprint** - UI, gameplay scripting, rapid prototyping
- **Rust 1.78+** - Data pipeline (World Bank, Open-Meteo APIs)
- **Python 3.11+** - Quick prototypes and scripts
- **SQLite 3.45+** - Game state, market data storage

## Key Directories
```
Source/ArgosyTides/       C++ game code
  Core/                   GameInstance, types, enums
  Data/                   DataManager, WeatherSystem
  Ship/                   Ship, FleetManager
  Economy/                (TODO) Market, commodities

Content/                  UE5 assets
  Blueprints/             Blueprint classes
  Maps/                   Game levels
  DataTables/             Data assets

Tools/
  DataPipeline/           Rust data fetcher
  fetch_data_prototype.py Python prototype

Config/                   UE5 configuration (.ini files)
docs/                     Design documents (GDD, TAD, ROADMAP)
```

## Coding Standards

### C++ (Unreal Engine)

**Naming Conventions:**
- Classes: `UArgosyTidesGameInstance`, `AShipActor`, `FCommodityPrice`
- Variables: `ShipName` (FString), `MaxCapacity` (int32), `bIsPlayerOwned` (bool)
- Functions: `StartNewGame()`, `GetCommodityPrice()`
- Use Hungarian notation: `F` (FString), `A` (Actor), `U` (UObject), `b` (bool)

**Required Macros:**
```cpp
UCLASS()                          // For UE5 classes
GENERATED_BODY()                  // In every UCLASS/USTRUCT
UPROPERTY()                       // For serialization, GC, Blueprint
UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable)      // Expose to Blueprint
```

**Types to Use:**
- `FString` (not std::string)
- `TArray<T>` (not std::vector)
- `TMap<K,V>` (not std::map)
- `int32`, `float`, `FDateTime` (UE5 types)
- `TSharedPtr`, `TWeakPtr` (for non-UObject)

**Logging:**
```cpp
UE_LOG(LogTemp, Log, TEXT("Message"));
UE_LOG(LogTemp, Warning, TEXT("Warning: %s"), *ErrorMessage);
UE_LOG(LogTemp, Error, TEXT("Error occurred"));
```

**Example Class:**
```cpp
// Ship.h
#pragma once
#include "CoreMinimal.h"
#include "UObject/Object.h"
#include "Ship.generated.h"

UCLASS()
class ARGOSYTIDES_API UShip : public UObject
{
    GENERATED_BODY()

public:
    UPROPERTY(BlueprintReadWrite, Category = "Identity")
    FString ShipName;

    UPROPERTY(BlueprintReadWrite, Category = "Stats")
    int32 MaxCargoCapacity;

    UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable, Category = "Cargo")
    bool LoadCargo(const FString& CommodityId, int32 Amount);
};
```

### Rust

**Standards:**
- Use `anyhow::Result` for application errors
- Use `thiserror` for library errors
- Use `tracing` crate for logging
- Use `?` operator for error propagation
- Rate limit API calls (500ms between requests)

**Example:**
```rust
use anyhow::Result;
use tracing::{info, warn, error};

pub async fn fetch_commodities(output_dir: &str) -> Result<()> {
    info!("Fetching commodity prices...");
    
    let client = Client::new();
    let response = client.get(&url).send().await?;
    
    if response.status().is_success() {
        info!("Fetch successful");
    } else {
        warn!("HTTP {}", response.status());
    }
    
    Ok(())
}
```

### Blueprint

**Standards:**
- Prefix with `BP_` (e.g., `BP_Ship`, `UI_PortScreen`)
- Inherit from C++ base classes when possible
- Add comments to complex logic graphs
- Test in PIE (Play In Editor) frequently

## Architecture Principles

### 1. Data Strategy (ADR-002)
```
Real-World APIs (World Bank, Open-Meteo)
    ↓
Calibration Layer (5% drift per game-week)
    ↓
Local Simulation (Supply/Demand)
    ↓
Gameplay Prices (What player sees)
```

**Key Point:** Real data calibrates the simulation, doesn't drive it directly.

### 2. Language Ownership (ADR-001)
- **C++:** Performance-critical, UE5 integration
- **Blueprint:** UI, designer-friendly, rapid iteration
- **Rust:** Data pipeline, CLI tools, compiled binary
- **Python:** Prototyping, one-off scripts

### 3. Layered Architecture
```
Game Layer (Blueprint/C++)
    ↓
Data Abstraction (UDataManager)
    ↓
Calibration (5% drift)
    ↓
Local Simulation
    ↓
Real-World APIs
```

## Common Patterns

### Data Manager Pattern
```cpp
UCLASS()
class UDataManager : public UObject {
    UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable)
    FCommodityPrice GetCommodityPrice(FString Id);
    
    UPROPERTY()
    TMap<FString, FCommodityPrice> CommodityCache;
    
    void FetchCommodityPrices();  // Internal API call
};
```

### Calibration Pattern
```cpp
// Gradual drift toward real data (5% per game-week)
void CalibratePrice(double& GamePrice, double RealPrice) {
    float DriftRate = 0.05f;
    GamePrice = FMath::Lerp(GamePrice, RealPrice, DriftRate);
}
```

### Event System
```cpp
DECLARE_DYNAMIC_MULTICAST_DELEGATE_TwoParams(
    FOnPriceChanged, FString, CommodityId, float, NewPrice
);

class UMarket {
    UPROPERTY(BlueprintAssignable)
    FOnPriceChanged OnPriceChanged;
};
```

## Build & Development

### Setup
```powershell
# Verify environment
.\setup.bat

# Open in Unreal Editor
ArgosyTides.uproject
```

### Building
```powershell
# Build UE5 project
.\build.bat

# Or manually
& "C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.4\Engine\Build\BatchFiles\Build.bat" `
  ArgosyTidesEditor Win64 Development `
  -project="ArgosyTides.uproject" -log -wait

# Build Rust pipeline
cd Tools\DataPipeline
cargo build --release

# Test Python prototype
python Tools\fetch_data_prototype.py --all
```

### Git Workflow
```powershell
# Stage changes
git add -A

# Commit with conventional commits
git commit -m "feat: add new ship class"
git commit -m "fix: resolve compilation error in DataManager"
git commit -m "docs: update README with build instructions"

# Push to remote
git push
```

